{{define "rubric"}}## Rating each idea
Rate every idea against {{if .Campaign}}the campaign{{else}}the workspace and its brand{{end}} on each criterion below, with a level from 1 to 5 and a reason of at most 12 words.
- First compare the ideas with each other, then rate. Keep level 5 for real standouts. If every idea is weak, rate them all low; do not spread the levels to look precise.
- When there is nothing to judge a criterion against ({{if .Campaign}}no key messages, no audience, no dates{{else}}no audience, no active campaigns{{end}}), rate it 3.
{{- range .Rubric.Criteria}}

**{{.Key}}** — {{.Question}}
{{- range .Anchors}}
- {{.}}
{{- end}}
{{- if eq .Hint "phase"}}
Also give "phase": the name of the phase it fits best.
{{- else if eq .Hint "campaign"}}
Also give "campaign": the name of the active campaign it would feed best, or leave it empty.
{{- end}}
{{- end}}

Then flag each cap that applies, whatever the levels. A capped idea is ranked low:
{{- range .Rubric.Caps}}
- {{.Cap}}: {{.Meaning}}
{{- end}}
Use an empty list when none applies.{{end}}

